<div class="data-source">
<p class="citation">Kushch, Volodymyr I., Sevostianov, Igor, Belyaev, A. S. (2015). Effective conductivity of spheroidal particle composite with imperfect interfaces: Complete solutions for periodic and random micro structures. Mechanics of Materials 89, 1-11. <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mechmat.2015.05.010">doi:10.1016/j.mechmat.2015.05.010</a></p>
<p><span class="label">Read in</span> Tables 1 to 8, pp. 6-9 <span class="badge ok">checked against the source</span></p>
<p><span class="label">Transcribed from</span> the published article (PDF), read on the page text</p>
<p class="note">Conductivities are divided by that of the matrix. All tables are for oblate spheroids of aspect ratio e = l3/l1 = 1/3, aligned with the axis x3. The low-conducting (Kapitza) interface has the parameter hc_tilde = l1 hc/k0 with the contrast k1/k0 = 1000; the highly conducting interface has hs_tilde = hs/(l1 k0) with k1/k0 = 0.1. The lattices are proportional: periods a1 = a2 and a3 = e a1; SP holds one spheroid per cell, BCP two (shift (a1, a2, a3)/2), FCP four (shifts (a1, 0, a3)/2, (a1, a2, 0)/2, (0, a2, a3)/2).</p>
</div>
